- cw: localReview and localResearch: two servers added on 2026-09-22 and 23. They have a local AI model (Ollama, on this machine) read code or text overnight. They do not touch the node.
- Why the servers still use the kernel: spirit.js hands it to them. It passes the kernel's functions on as spirit.core.
- The fix:
  - spirit.js stops passing them on;
  - the same functions live on spirit itself, built on its one post: spirit.jobs.publish, spirit.peerPost;
  - the servers call those;
  - spirit.js no longer loads the kernel.

- cw: today, nothing would start:
